Rule 5 (breakpoints as a tuple of integers must be within the valid index range of the detrend axis)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : tuple(int)} |= if v_2 ≥ 0 then (∀i ∈ [0, v_3.len - 1] : v_3[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_3[i] < shape(v_1, v_2)) else (∀i ∈ [0, v_3.len - 1] : v_3[i] ≥ 0 ∧ v_3[i] < shape(v_1, v_2 + ndim(v_1)))
>>
Rule 6 (breakpoint as a single integer must be within the valid index range of the detrend axis)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int, v_3 : int} |= if v_2 ≥ 0 then v_3 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 < shape(v_1, v_2) else v_3 ≥ 0 ∧ v_3 < shape(v_1, v_2 + ndim(v_1))
